<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ethiopian People's Revolutionary Democratic Front</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1988–2019</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as EPRDF</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ethiopian People's Revolutionary Democratic Front (EPRDF) was a coalition of ethnic-based parties led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigray-peoples-liberation-front">Tigray People's Liberation Front</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meles-zenawi">Meles Zenawi</a>. Its forces overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a> regime in May 1991, and it then governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> under the ethnic federal constitution of 1994, presiding over rapid state-led growth while restricting opposition and the press. In 2019 Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abiy-ahmed">Abiy Ahmed</a> merged most of it into the new Prosperity Party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ethiopian-peoples-revolutionary-democratic-front.jpg" alt="Ethiopian People's Revolutionary Democratic Front" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: IvY88 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_Ethiopia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
